  "letters": [
   {
    "n": 169,
    "year": 1647,
    "date": "February 20, 1647",
    "place": "Milan",
    "archival": "ARSI, FG 745, 28",
    "excerpt": "For a long time now the fire has lain hidden under the ashes; but now that so many go to spend their labors, some to Chile, some to Japan — and would God that among these my name might be read — it has grown so that without uncovering it, it would cause no small distress in a soul, it being proper for fire to rise on high, scorning these mortal things. Having suffered much in the novitiate, and this, as I believe, being caused by the change of air from Milan to that of Genoa, they came to the decision to dismiss me from the Company so beloved by me; their designs did not take effect, for my soul, too fervent in its thoughts, they thought perhaps to find a heart of flesh, but found it of diamond, still maintaining the designs of my superiors, the infernal enemy firm; I had recourse to my St.",
    "kind": "abridged",
    "full_paras": [
     "For a long time now the fire has lain hidden under the ashes; but now that so many go to spend their labors, some to Chile, some to Japan — and would God that among these my name might be read — it has grown so that without uncovering it, it would cause no small distress in a soul, it being proper for fire to rise on high, scorning these mortal things. Having suffered much in the novitiate, and this, as I believe, being caused by the change of air from Milan to that of Genoa, they came to the decision to dismiss me from the Company so beloved by me; their designs did not take effect, for my soul, too fervent in its thoughts, they thought perhaps to find a heart of flesh, but found it of diamond, still maintaining the designs of my superiors, the infernal enemy firm; I had recourse to my St. Francis, promising to follow him if he would grant me health; Heaven willed that barely five months should pass before, my former health being confirmed, I made, on the day of Blessed Aloysius three years ago, the vows. The fire has ever lain hidden; but now, Father, it has become so great that it could not wait so long to write four lines wherein it has in part wished to be uncovered. I know I am understood by Your Paternity without my explaining myself in words [...]; but to better obtain the license, I pray Your Paternity to grant me leave to go to Chile. Ah, Father, by the bowels of Christ, do not let me be defrauded of the one hope I hold of obtaining from Your Paternity what I desire; but in case I were not heard, I would pray — but I hope in the charity of Your Paternity and in my St. Francis that I shall obtain the grace I desire — not to speak of it with any person. I am now studying logic. In closing, sure of obtaining the grace, I humbly reverence you."
    ]
   }
  ]
